@page "/docs/support"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Support — Vaultex</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">Resources</div>
<h1>Support</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Stuck on something? Here's how to get help.
</p>

<h2 id="self-serve">Self-serve</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Search this documentation &mdash; press <code>Ctrl K</code> from anywhere.</li>
    <li>Check the <a href="/docs/errors">error reference</a> for what a specific OAuth code means.</li>
    <li>Read the <a href="/docs/changelog">changelog</a> for recent behaviour changes.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="community">Community</h2>
<ul>
    <li>GitHub discussions for design questions and feature requests.</li>
    <li>Stack Overflow with the <code>vaultex</code> tag for code-level questions.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="paid">Paid support</h2>
<p>
    Customers on a paid plan can email <a href="mailto:support@vaultex.io">support@vaultex.io</a>
    or open a ticket from the admin portal under <strong>Help → Contact support</strong>. Median
    response time is under 4 business hours.
</p>

<h2 id="security">Security</h2>
<p>
    Found a vulnerability? Email <a href="mailto:security@vaultex.io">security@vaultex.io</a>. Please
    don't open a public issue. We follow a 90-day responsible-disclosure policy and credit reporters
    in our changelog.
</p>

